amux do new-workgroup — create a workgroup (and a first agent when repos are given)

usage: amux do new-workgroup [-f key=value]...

fields (-f key=value, repeatable):
  name=<text>                workgroup display name
  prompt=<text>              the coordinator's task (its goal on the default runtime); never copied to a member
  repos=<a,b>                repos the workgroup is limited to (its grant ceiling); naming any also creates
                             a first member agent on them (one repo = a single-repo workgroup)
  agent=<harness>            first member's harness: claude | codex (default claude)
  model=<model>              first member's model (default: its harness's default)
  mode=<mode>                first member's mode: task | interactive (default task)
  coordinator=<harness>      coordinator runtime: claude | codex (default codex, the native goal runtime;
                             claude runs in goal mode through amux's goal hooks)
  coordinator_model=<model>  coordinator model (default: its harness's default)
  linear=<url>               Linear issue link, prepended to the prompt

examples:
  amux do new-workgroup -f name=infra -f repos=infra -f prompt="upgrade CI"
  amux do new-workgroup -f name=triage -f coordinator=claude -f coordinator_model=opus
